//! Status-change webhooks.
//!
//! When a credential's status flips ([`crate::status::revoke_credential`]),
//! [`Notifier::notify`] sends the change to the relying parties that
//! subscribed to the issuing tenant's changes. A subscription is a tenant
//! setting of kind [`WEBHOOK_KIND`] whose value holds the endpoint `url`.
//!
//! Deliveries run concurrently, at most [`MAX_CONCURRENT_DELIVERIES`] at a
//! time, each bounded by [`DELIVERY_TIMEOUT`], and the whole change by
//! [`DISPATCH_BUDGET`]. There are no retries: every subscriber gets exactly
//! one [`DeliveryEvent`] in the [`DeliverySink`], and one that is not
//! delivered, including one not reached before the budget ran out, is
//! recorded as [`Outcome::Failed`].
//!
//! The canary is a platform subscription on the instance's loopback that
//! receives every change, sent after the subscriber lookup through the same
//! transport as the change's subscribers. [`Notifier::canary_healthy`] is the
//! notifier's health check: green only if, for the most recent change, the
//! canary acknowledged and every subscriber was looked up and attempted
//! within the budget. A relying party's own failure is reported in its
//! delivery event, not in the health check.

